{
  "name": "Retry Effects · 1 Guarded call",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Retry Effects · Guarded call\nA sub-workflow that makes one outside call at most once per `key`, however often the execution is retried.\n\nCall it from an **Execute Sub-workflow** node set to **Run once for each item**. Each item needs a `key` that is the same on every attempt (order id + line, event id + recipient). Do not build it from `$execution.id`: a retry gets a new execution id.\n\n**Why a sub-workflow:** when a retry starts at a failed node, the nodes before it do not run again, so a check placed in front of the call is skipped. A failed Execute Sub-workflow node runs the whole sub-workflow again, check included.\n\nIt answers with `outcome`: `sent`, `already_done`, `found_at_service`, `held`, or `busy` (another run took this key at the same moment).\n\nReplace **Call the service** with your own node and keep its **On Error** on *Continue (using error output)*. Replace **Look it up** too, or stay on `hold`. Settings are at the top of **Entry**.",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 480,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "907b0374-1445-4da6-83f1-a95f12cd89bf",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -620
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### The ledger row\n- `sending`: a run is in the middle of the call. Another run that meets it answers `busy`. After `LEASE_SECONDS` it counts as a run that died, and is treated as `unknown`.\n- `done`: the service answered. Later runs answer `already_done` and do not call.\n- `unknown`: the call failed or timed out. Nobody knows if the service did the work.\n\n### What happens to `unknown`\n- `hold` (default): do not call. The item comes back with `outcome: held` for a person to check. To release it, set the row to `done`, or delete it to send again.\n- `lookup`: ask the service with **Look it up**. Found: mark done, no call. A clear \"not there\": call again. Any other answer: hold.\n\nUse `lookup` only when the service shows a write the moment it happens. A lookup that lags will say \"not there\" about something that is.",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 420,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "33c51962-c7fb-43a6-8924-73f9a923e75e",
      "name": "Unknown",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        900,
        -620
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "inputSource": "passthrough"
      },
      "id": "f2953808-5d5f-4de6-8b31-2730579780cf",
      "name": "When called",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Settings.\nconst ON_UNKNOWN = 'hold'; // 'hold' or 'lookup', see the note. An item can override it with on_unknown.\nconst LEASE_SECONDS = 300; // a row still \"sending\" after this long counts as a run that died. Set it longer than your slowest call.\n\nconst input = $input.first().json;\nconst key = String(input.key ?? '').trim();\nif (!key) throw new Error('Guarded call needs a key on the item');\nconst hex = () => Math.floor(Math.random() * 0x100000000).toString(16).padStart(8, '0');\n// token: this run. It tells my ledger rows from those of a run that started at the same moment.\nreturn [{ json: { key, payload: input.payload ?? {}, on_unknown: input.on_unknown ?? ON_UNKNOWN, lease_seconds: LEASE_SECONDS, token: `${$execution.id}-${hex()}${hex()}` } }];"
      },
